sequenceDiagram
autonumber
participant U as unary()
participant C as TrendConfig
participant D as RuntimeTrendDetector
participant F as runtime_trend functions
U->>C: validate parameters and UI defaults
U->>D: construct(config)
loop each timestamp_ns and value
    U->>D: update_ns(timestamp_ns, value)
    Note over D: Require strictly increasing integer nanoseconds
    Note over D: Keep bounded time window, reset streak after large gap
    U->>D: evaluate()
    alt same timestamp already evaluated
        D-->>U: cached TrendResult, no confirmation advance
    else new timestamp
        alt samples and coverage sufficient
            D->>F: _fit(x_minutes from integer time differences, scaled_y, config)
            F-->>D: slope, residual variance, cleaned values
            D->>F: _step_like(x, cleaned, config)
            F-->>D: step flag
            Note over D: Gate by step, variance, tangent, update direction streak
        else insufficient coverage
            Note over D: reason=warmup, ready=false
        end
        D-->>U: runtime_trend.TrendResult(ready, detected, reason)
    end
    Note over U: Store float(detected) = 0/1 if ready, otherwise None
end
